uting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-09T18:31:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 091831 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1231 PM MDT Fri Oct 9 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Terrain-driven showers and thunderstorms and unseasonably warm temperatures continue today. - A pattern change arrives this weekend bringing another round of tropical moisture to the region bringing flood potential to the region. - Heavy with totals of 1-3","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-09T08:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Critical fire weather conditions are not expected to develop. Isolated showers and thunderstorms are possible on the Uintas and the Central Mountains of CO this afternoon. A surge in moisture this weekend, due to extra-tropical moisture will lead to wetting rains and flash flooding concerns around sensitive terrain. Unsettled weather likely sticks around well into next week. ...GUST","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"mkr01","station_name":"Meeker","distance_km":3.3,"soil_temp_5cm_f":52.36,"soil_temp_15cm_f":55.38,"soil_moisture_5cm":